  "narrative": "This brief looks at moving anndata to NumPy 2.0, tested under NumPy 2.0.2 compared with 1.26.4 before. NumPy 2.0 removes 63 public names. Only two of those are used in this code, namely numpy.NaN and numpy.string_, so only those two can break this package. Three other names in use are deprecated but still work, and there are three flags for changed behavior around numeric types and type promotion.\n\nNo part of the code fails at import, though 17 additional modules are flagged as at risk if the removed names are reached at run time. The single verified worst chain is clean and matches the observed failure, which means no broken chain of modules was found starting from import.\n\nEvidence confidence is high for import health. Both checks found that import still succeeds under NumPy 2.0.2, each with a score of 1.00.\n\nFix the two removed names first, replacing uses of numpy.NaN and numpy.string_ with their NumPy 2.0 equivalents, then review the at risk modules and the changed numeric behavior. The deprecated names can wait since they still function.",
